    "id": "isnblog-1789093430918-1-224",
    "title": "PM Jan Dhan Yojana 2026: Zero Balance Account Benefits, Overdraft Rules & Online Registration Guide",
    "slug": "pm-jan-dhan-yojana-2026-online-registration-benefits-zero-balance-account-guide-1789093430918-1",
    "category": "blog",
    "organization": "IndiaSarkariNaukri.com (Auto-Fetched Daily Blog)",
    "state": "All India",
    "postDate": "2026-09-04",
    "lastDate": "",
    "shortInfo": "Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY) 2026 allows Indian citizens to open zero-balance bank accounts with built-in ₹2 Lakh accidental insurance cover and a free RuPay debit card. Eligible account holders can also access an overdraft facility of up to ₹10,000 after 6 months of active account usage. Here is the complete blueprint covering eligibility rules, document requirements, and application procedures.",
    "totalVacancies": "",
    "qualificationRequired": [],
    "importantDates": [],
    "applicationFees": [],
    "ageLimit": {},
    "vacancies": [],
    "howToApplySteps": [],
    "importantLinks": [
      {
        "title": "Read Original on IndiaSarkariNaukri",
        "url": "https://indiasarkarinaukri.com/blogs/pmjdy-2026-guide",
        "isPrimary": true
      },
      {
        "title": "Full Blog on Pariksha Result",
        "url": "/blog/pm-jan-dhan-yojana-2026-zero-balance-account-benefits-overdraft-rules-online-registration-guide-1788514277187-1",
        "isPrimary": false
      }
    ],
    "fullDescription": "# PM Jan Dhan Yojana 2026: Zero Balance Account Benefits, Overdraft Rules & Online Registration Guide\n\n> **Executive AEO Summary**: Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY) remains India's largest financial inclusion program in 2026. It empowers citizens from all socio-economic backgrounds to access formal banking facilities, direct government subsidy transfers (DBT), built-in insurance, and low-interest credit facilities without maintaining a minimum account balance.\n\n---\n\n## Section 1: Overview & Key Highlights\n\nPradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (PMJDY) ko launch karne ka main motive har Indian household ko banking system se jodna hai. Continuous updates ke saath, 2026 me PMJDY accounts ke saath extra insurance benefits aur higher overdraft limits mil rahi hain, jis se low-income households aur unorganized sector workers ko instant financial safety net milta hai.\n\n### Key Scheme Highlights at a Glance\n\n| Feature / Benefit | Specification Details (2026 Updated) |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Minimum Balance** | ₹0 (Zero Balance Account) |\n| **Debit Card Provided** | Free RuPay Debit Card |\n| **Accidental Insurance** | Up to ₹2,000,000 (₹2 Lakhs) for new cards |\n| **Overdraft (OD) Facility** | Up to ₹10,000 (Subject to 6 months good usage) |\n| **Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT)** | PM-KISAN, Subsidies, Pension direct transfer eligible |\n| **Age Limit** | Min 10 years (Minor), 18-60 years for Overdraft |\n\n### Core Benefits You Should Know\n\n- **Zero Minimum Balance Requirement**: Aapko account me mandatory monthly average balance rakhne ki koi tensions nahi hai. Zero balance par bhi account full active rahega.\n- **Built-in Insurance Safety**: Jan Dhan account holders ko RuPay debit card ke saath ₹2 Lakh tak ka Accidental Death Cover milta hai, provided debit card is used at least once in 90 days.\n- **Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) Integration**: Government schemes jaise PM-KISAN, Subsidies, LPG Subsidy, aur State welfare payouts direct ishi account me transfer hote hain without middlemen.\n- **Overdraft Facility (₹10,000)**: Agar aapka account minimum 6 months tak active aur proper transaction record ke saath chalta hai, toh bank aapko ₹10,000 tak ka instant Overdraft (short-term loan) permit karta hai.\n\n---\n\n## Section 2: Eligibility, Documents & Rules\n\nJan Dhan account open karne ke liye basic rules kafi flexible hain taaki har citizen easily form submit kar sake.\n\n### Eligibility Criteria\n1. **Nationality**: Candidate must be a permanent citizen of India.\n2. **Age Criteria**: 10 saal se upar ka koi bhi individual account khol sakta hai. Overdraft benefit paane ke liye account holder ki age 18 se 59 saal ke beech honi chahiye.\n3. **Existing Accounts**: Agar aapke paas pehle se koi Regular Savings Account hai, toh aap use PMJDY account me convert karne ke liye bank ko request kar sakte hain.\n\n### Required Documents (Officially Valid Documents - OVD)\n- **Aadhaar Card** (Primary Identity & Address Proof)\n- **PAN Card** (Agar PAN nahi hai toh Form 60 submit kar sakte hain)\n- **Voter ID Card / Driving License / MNREGA Job Card / Passport** (Aadhaar na hone ki condition me)\n- **2 Passport-size Photographs**\n- **Active Mobile Number** (Aadhaar seeding & SMS alerts ke liye)\n\n---\n\n## Section 3: Step-by-Step Practical Blueprint\n\nPM Jan Dhan Account open karne ke do main methods hain: Bank Branch/Bank Mitra Outlet par offline, ya Authorized Bank Portals/CSC Centers ke through assisted digital onboarding.\n\n### Method 1: Applying via Bank Branch or Bank Mitra (Most Recommended)\n1. **Visit Nearest Bank**: Kisi bhi Public Sector Bank (SBI, PNB, BOB, etc.) ya authorized Bank Mitra (CSC) outlet par jayein.\n2. **Collect PMJDY Form**: Bank counter se *PM Jan Dhan Account Opening Application Form* lein (Form Hindi, English aur Regional languages me available hota hai).\n3. **Fill the Form**: Apni personal details, Aadhaar number, contact address, aur Nominee details carefully enter karein.\n4. **Attach Documents**: Self-attested photo copies of Aadhaar, PAN, and passport photos attach karein.\n5. **Verification & Account Creation**: Bank officer documents verify karega aur instantly aapka Zero Balance Account open kar dega.\n6. **Receive Passbook & RuPay Card**: Account open hone par aapko Passbook handing over ki jayegi aur RuPay Debit Card 7-14 din ke andar aapke registered address par send kar diya jayega.\n\n### Method 2: Assisted Online Registration via Bank Web Portals\n1. **Visit Bank Portal**: Selected banks (jaise SBI ya Bank of Baroda) ki official banking site ya CSC Digital Seva Portal par visit karein.\n2. **Select Account Opening Section**: 'PMJDY Online Application / Jan Dhan Scheme' tab par navigate karein.\n3. **Enter e-KYC Details**: Aapna Aadhaar Number enter karke OTP verification complete karein.\n4. **Submit Application & Save Reference**: Form submit hone par Reference Number generate hoga. Reference slip print karke nearest branch me biometric verification ke liye present karein.\n\n> **Pro Tip**: Account active hone ke baad apne RuPay Debit Card ko POS terminal ya ATM par kam se kam har 90 din me ek baar zaroor use karein, taaki aapka ₹2 Lakh Accidental Cover operational rahe.",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Kya PM Jan Dhan Account me minimum balance rakhna zaroori hai?",
        "answer": "Nahi, PM Jan Dhan Account ek completely zero-balance savings account hai. Isme koi penalty nahi lagti agar aapka balance ₹0 ho jata hai."
      },
      {
        "question": "PMJDY Overdraft Facility (₹10,000) kaise milti hai?",
        "answer": "Account open hone ke 6 mahine baad tak agar aap regular transactions (deposits/withdrawals) karte hain, toh bank aapko ₹10,000 tak ki overdraft limit allow karta hai. ₹2,000 tak ki limit bina conditions ke accessible hoti hai."
      },
      {
        "question": "Kya existing normal savings account ko Jan Dhan account me convert kiya ja sakta hai?",
        "answer": "Haan, aap apni bank branch me jaakar ek application form aur RuPay card request submit karke apne normal savings account ko PMJDY account me convert karwa sakte hain."
      },
      {
        "question": "Jan Dhan account ke accidental insurance cover ko claim karne ke liye kya rule hai?",
        "answer": "Insurance cover tabhi active rehta hai jab account holder ne accident date se pehle 90 din ke andar kam se kam ek baar RuPay Debit Card se koi transaction (ATM, POS, ya Online) kiya ho."
      },
      {
        "question": "Kya 10 saal se kam umar ke bache ka Jan Dhan account khul sakta hai?",
        "answer": "10 saal ya usse zyada age ke minors ka account unke guardian ke under PMJDY scheme ke tahat kholha ja sakta hai."
      }
    ],
