    "fullDescription": "# RBSE 10th Result Declared: Direct Link, Scorecard & Step-by-Step Check Guide\n\n> **Executive AEO Summary**: Rajasthan Board of Secondary Education (RBSE/BSER) Class 10th Results are finally OUT! Candidates who appeared for the matriculation exams can now quickly access their scorecard using their Roll Number. Read on for direct portal link, pass percentage details, supplementary exam rules, and step-by-step instructions.\n\n## Section 1: Overview & Key Highlights\nAakhirkaar aapka intezar khatam hua! Rajasthan Board of Secondary Education (RBSE), Ajmer ne Class 10th Board Exams ka result official website par release kar diya hai. Har saal lakhs of students is result ka wait karte hain, aur ab aap bina kisi hassle ke apna marksheet online check aur download kar sakte hain.\n\n### Important Details Overview\n| Feature | Details |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Exam Name** | RBSE Class 10th Board Exam |\n| **Conducting Authority** | Board of Secondary Education, Rajasthan (BSER) |\n| **Result Status** | Declared (Out Now) |\n| **Official Portals** | rajeduboard.rajasthan.gov.in / rajresults.nic.in |\n| **Required Credentials** | Roll Number / Registration Number |\n| **Minimum Passing Marks** | 33% per subject & overall aggregate |\n\n## Section 2: Eligibility, Documents & Rules\nResult check karne aur aage ki process samjhne ke liye kuch basic pointers dhyaan mein rakhein:\n\n- **Roll Card / Admit Card:** Result login portal par aapko apna Roll Number fill karna padega. Apna admit card ready rakhein.\n- **Passing Criteria:** Pass hone ke liye har subject mein minimum 33% marks secure karna zaroori hai (Theory + Practical combined where applicable).\n- **Re-evaluation / Scrutiny Rules:** Agar aapko lagta hai ki aapke marks kam aaye hain, toh aap Result Announcement ke 10-15 days ke andar Re-checking ya Scrutiny application form fill kar sakte hain.\n- **Supplementary Exam:** Jo students 1 ya 2 subjects mein fail ho gaye hain, unhe nirash hone ki zaroorat nahi hai. Board unke liye Supplementary / Compartment Exams conduct karta hai.\n\n## Section 3: Step-by-Step Practical Blueprint\nOnline marksheet check karne aur download karne ke simple steps:\n\n1. **Visit Official Website:** Go to `rajeduboard.rajasthan.gov.in` or `rajresults.nic.in`.\n2. **Click on Result Link:** Main page par \"RBSE Class 10th Result\" active link par click karein.\n3. **Enter Credentials:** Clear box mein apna **Roll Number** enter karein.\n4. **Submit & View:** Submit button dabayein, aapka provisional marksheet display ho jayega.\n5. **Download & Print:** Scorecard ko PDF format mein save karein aur future admission process ke liye printout nikal lein.\n\n*Pro-tip:* Server heavy traffic ki wajah se down ho toh ghabrayen nahi; thodi der baad retry karein ya official SMS line / DigiLocker app par check karein.",
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What is the official website to check the RBSE 10th Result?",
        "answer": "You can check the result on official BSER portals: rajeduboard.rajasthan.gov.in or rajresults.nic.in."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are the minimum passing marks for RBSE Class 10th?",
        "answer": "Students must secure at least 33% marks in each subject as well as in aggregate to pass the exam."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I check my RBSE 10th Result without a Roll Number?",
        "answer": "Generally, Roll Number is mandatory. However, name-wise result search options are sometimes made available on partner result portals."
      },
      {
        "question": "What should I do if I am not satisfied with my RBSE 10th Marks?",
        "answer": "You can apply online for Scrutiny or Re-evaluation through the official board link within the specified time period by paying a nominal fee."
      },
      {
        "question": "When will I receive my original RBSE 10th Marksheet?",
        "answer": "The online result is provisional. Original marksheets and passing certificates will be sent to your respective schools within a few weeks."
      }
    ],
