    "fullContent": "The Executive Board of the Sahitya Akademi has declared the names of the recipients of the Sahitya Akademi Yuva Puraskar and Bal Sahitya Puraskar for the year 2026. These awards celebrate exceptional creative writing by authors below the age of 35 (Yuva Puraskar) and recognize path-breaking literary works dedicated to children's literature (Bal Sahitya Puraskar). The awards span across various genres including poetry, short stories, novels, and essays written in 22 languages recognized by the Constitution of India, alongside English and Rajasthani. Notable works this year touch upon contemporary social realities, folk folklore preservation, and ecological themes aimed at cultivating reading habits among younger demographics. Each winner will be honored with a casket containing an engraved copper-plaque and a cash prize of Rs 50,000 at a special awards ceremony later this year. Exam Relevance: Important for UPSC, State PSCs, and SSC examinations where questions regarding national literary awards, cultural bodies, and regional language recognition are frequently asked.",
