    "keyHighlights": [
      "Achieved hypersonic cruise speeds exceeding Mach 6 at high altitudes.",
      "Utilizes an indigenous air-breathing scramjet propulsion system.",
      "Paves the way for development of advanced hypersonic cruise missiles."
    ],
    "fullContent": "The Defence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO) has achieved a stellar breakthrough in indigenous defense manufacturing with the successful flight test of the Hypersonic Technology Demonstrator Vehicle (HSTDV). Launched from the Dr APJ Abdul Kalam Island off the coast of Odisha, the demonstrator achieved a cruising speed in excess of Mach 6 (six times the speed of sound) and maintained stable flight parameters for the designated duration. The core of the HSTDV is an advanced air-breathing scramjet (supersonic combustion ramjet) engine. Unlike conventional rocket-powered missiles that carry both fuel and heavy oxidizer tanks, scramjet technology harvests oxygen directly from the atmospheric air during flight, drastically reducing weapon weight and increasing range and speed payload efficiency. This successful trial acts as a foundational block for developing futuristic long-range hypersonic cruise missiles and rapid-deployment reusable space launch systems. Exam Relevance: High priority for NDA, CDS, CAPF, and civil services exams focusing on indigenous defense technology and strategic military advancements.",
