    "date": "11 September 2026",
    "category": "Science & Space",
    "summary": "The Indian Space Research Organisation (ISRO) has successfully conducted a hot-fire test of its newly developed 2000 kN semi-cryogenic rocket engine. This milestone engine uses environmentally sustainable liquid oxygen and refined kerosene, promising higher payload capacities for future lunar and interplanetary missions.",
