    "fullContent": "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) has formally rolled out the 11th cohort of its Regulatory Sandbox, focusing specifically on 'Cross-Border CBDC Interoperability and Offline Retail Solutions'. This move underscores the central bank's proactive stance in expanding the utility and global footprint of the Digital Rupee (e-Rupee). **Scope of the 11th Cohort** Selected fintech firms and banking consortia will test innovative technologies designed to bridge India's CBDC infrastructure with payment systems of major partner economies. The trials will evaluate mechanisms to lower remittance costs, reduce settlement times from days to seconds, and ensure robust security using cryptographic tools like zero-knowledge proofs. **Significance for Monetary Policy** While pilot projects for retail and wholesale e-Rupee have achieved significant transaction milestones domestically, this cohort addresses the complex challenge of cross-border compliance, foreign exchange controls, and multi-currency ledger syncing. **Exam Relevance** Banking and SSC aspirants should note the specific focus areas of RBI regulatory sandbox cohorts, particularly terms related to CBDC, fintech innovations, and payment system architectures.",
