    "fullContent": "### PM E-DRIVE Scheme Phase-II Approval In a major push toward clean mobility and achieving Net Zero targets by 2070, the Union Cabinet, chaired by the Prime Minister, has approved the second phase of the **PM Electric Drive Revolution in Innovative Vehicle Enhancement (PM E-DRIVE) Scheme**. The initiative replaces the erstwhile FAME-II framework with a more targeted approach toward public transport decarbonization and ecosystem building. #### Financial Outlay and Resource Allocation The scheme carries a total financial outlay of **₹10,900 crore** over a two-year operational period. Out of this total allocation, **₹3,679 crore** has been earmarked for subsidies for electric two-wheelers (e-2Ws), electric three-wheelers (e-3Ws), e-ambulances, and e-trucks. To address range anxiety among EV owners, **₹2,000 crore** is set aside for establishing charging infrastructure across high-density national highways and metropolitan cities. #### Key Objectives and Fleet Targets 1. **Public Transport Acceleration:** The scheme targets funding for **14,028 electric buses** to be deployed by state transport undertakings (STUs) through CESL procurement. 2. **Charging Infrastructure:** Installation of 22,100 fast chargers for e-4Ws, 1,800 fast chargers for e-buses, and 48,400 target chargers for e-2Ws/3Ws. 3. **Test Infrastructure Upgrade:** Allocation of **₹780 crore** for modernizing test agencies under the Ministry of Heavy Industries. #### Significance for Competitive Exams For UPSC, SSC, and Banking exams, candidates should note that the PM E-DRIVE scheme operates under the **Ministry of Heavy Industries**. It incorporates the **Phased Manufacturing Programme (PMP)** to promote the 'Make in India' initiative in battery cell manufacturing and EV powertrain components. Questions regarding electric vehicle schemes usually focus on nodal ministries, budgetary allocations, target vehicle segments, and environmental commitments under COP26 goals.",
