    "fullContent": "### Summit Context and Overview On September 4, 2026, the Ministry of External Affairs hosted the **6th Indo-Pacific Oceans Initiative (IPOI) Summit** in New Delhi. Representatives, diplomats, and defense experts from 18 Indo-Pacific countries gathered to address emerging maritime challenges, freedom of navigation, and marine ecological conservation. ### Key Outcomes & Frameworks The centerpiece of the summit was the unanimous adoption of the **Indo-Pacific Blue Economy Framework (IP-BEF)**. This framework outlines joint operational protocols for: 1. **Maritime Security:** Enhancing real-time Information Fusion Centre – Indian Ocean Region (IFC-IOR) data sharing. 2. **Marine Resources:** Combatting Illegal, Unreported, and Unregulated (IUU) fishing through satellite-based vessel tracking. 3. **Disaster Risk Reduction:** Establishing rapid-response humanitarian assistance protocols across island nations. India also pledged a **$100 million Maritime Infrastructure Assistance Fund** aimed at developing climate-resilient port infrastructure in ASEAN countries. ### Background of IPOI First proposed by India’s Prime Minister at the 14th East Asia Summit in Bangkok in November 2019, IPOI rests on **seven pillars**: Maritime Security, Maritime Ecology, Maritime Resources, Capacity Building, Disaster Risk Reduction, Science & Tech Cooperation, and Trade Connectivity. ### Exam Relevance * **UPSC GS Paper-II:** Bilateral, regional, and global groupings involving India and affecting India's interests. * **Key Concepts:** SAGAR Vision (Security and Growth for All in the Region), IFC-IOR, and UNCLOS alignment.",
